[SLICE]
UID: SLICE-CHECKPOINT-WIRING
TITLE: Wire the behaviour model into the CLI and the checkpoints
DEPTH: needs-design
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Add the lifecycle verbs to the CLI: a move is a command that selects one
transition, checks its gates, and either refuses with a diagnostic or writes.
Register the existing checks -- fingerprint drift, cycles, plan boundaries,
the authorship guard -- as validators at the checkpoints the model derives for
them: the command before and after its write, the pre-commit hook against the
previous commit, CI against the merge base, and strictdoc's read seam and
post-index hook as backstops for edits that bypass the CLI. Fail the
evaluation when a gate has no validator, or no checkpoint that can see what it
needs.

Consumer surface the operator reviews before implementation: the checkpoint
table -- which check runs where, and what is still unenforceable. Reviewed
after: a rule that used to live in the skill being refused by a running check.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
This is the milestone INV-GUARDS-MUST-EXECUTE asks for. Measured: strictdoc's
hook never runs on node creation, so it is a backstop; the read seam fires on
every command; checks that need the previous state cannot run at command time
by construction; checks that need to know who is acting can run only in the
acting session until agents have their own identity.
<<<
PARENT_FP: DEC-EXECUTABLE-RULES-ROADMAP:0000000
NOTES: >>>
A flow's tests become its contract once its mechanics settle, per
MECH-TESTS-AS-CONTRACT.
<<<
