[SLICE]
UID: SLICE-INSTANCE-SEMANTICS-MIGRATION
TITLE: Migrate this system's own semantics onto the plumbing
DEPTH: needs-design
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Express fingerprints, acceptance, the ripple, DEPTH and the two keys in the
behaviour model, and retire the hand-written scripts they live in today: the
contract-field selection as the model's read scopes; a signed edge as a
milestone whose evidence goes stale when a parent's contract changes;
readiness and degrees of freedom as gates over the closure; signing and the
authorship flip as moves with an actor rule; revocation made visible. The
decisions this milestone needs are the instance's own -- who may sign, whether
DEPTH may move backwards, whether implemented and verified belong in DEPTH,
agent identity -- and are taken at its review, not before.

Consumer surface the operator reviews before implementation: the instance's
lifecycle rendered from the model, with those decisions marked. Reviewed
after: the existing fingerprint and readiness checks passing through the new
validators with identical results on the real graph.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Migration last keeps the open instance decisions from blocking the plumbing,
and the plumbing is what makes those decisions reviewable rather than guessed.
<<<
PARENT_FP: >>>
DEC-EXECUTABLE-RULES-ROADMAP:0000000
DEC-FINGERPRINT-IN-NODE:0000000
DEC-FP-ACCEPT-AUTHORITY:0000000
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Git-flow handling -- rebase, squash lineage, pre-merge collection -- stays
deferred until a branch reaches main, per MECH-FP-GIT-FLOW-HAZARDS.
<<<
